  "bio": [
    "I build and analyze mathematical and AI models of complex systems: AI and agentic systems, infectious disease transmission, vaccine trials, network resilience. My work spans agent-based simulation of hepatitis C among people who inject drugs, scalable network generation, interdiction and recovery on networks, and non-probabilistic risk management for AI.",
    "I held an adjunct professor appointment in the Department of Medicine at Loyola University Chicago, with an appointment in the Division of Epidemiology & Biostatistics at the University of Illinois Chicago. Earlier positions were at the U.S. FDA, the University of Texas at Austin and Los Alamos National Laboratory. I received my PhD in Applied Mathematics from Cornell University.",
    "Research with my collaborators has been supported by over $9M in grants from NIH, CDC and FDA, and has appeared in venues including Science Translational Medicine, PNAS Nexus, PLOS ONE and Scientific Reports."
  ],
